From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PipelineCache: inherit the device's current stencil reference

GraphicsDevice.ReferenceStencil can override the reference without mutating
the bound DepthStencilState. When an effect changes another depth/stencil
field, BeginApplyDepthStencil seeds the replacement state from that bound
object, losing the dynamic reference even if the effect never sets it.

Meridian: New World uses this path for terrain lighting. In a captured
frame, the reference changes from 220 to zero when depth writes are enabled
for a later effect. The NotEqual stencil test then rejects the terrain's
direct-light draw against the cleared buffer. Preserving the three affected
references in an otherwise unchanged frame capture restores the lighting.

Inherit the effective device reference, including any pending state handled
by the preceding GraphicsDevice ordering fix. Explicit STENCILREF effect
states still replace it through the existing effect-state parser. Keep the
caller's state object immutable and the reference in the pipeline cache key.

This is a GE-Proton downstream patch, not an upstream FNA submission.
Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/430
---
diff --git a/src/Graphics/PipelineCache.cs b/src/Graphics/PipelineCache.cs
--- a/src/Graphics/PipelineCache.cs
+++ b/src/Graphics/PipelineCache.cs
@@ -389,7 +389,8 @@ namespace Microsoft.Xna.Framework.Graphics
 			CCWStencilDepthBufferFail = oldDepthStencilState.CounterClockwiseStencilDepthBufferFail;
 			StencilMask = oldDepthStencilState.StencilMask;
 			StencilWriteMask = oldDepthStencilState.StencilWriteMask;
-			ReferenceStencil = oldDepthStencilState.ReferenceStencil;
+			// Effects inherit the dynamic reference unless the pass overrides it.
+			ReferenceStencil = device.ReferenceStencil;
 		}
 
 		public void EndApplyDepthStencil()
